{"Timing race condition in test_basic: background threads may not complete before assertions - the time.sleep(0.1) is insufficient guarantee that the flusher has completed all work, and the test passes inconsistently due to race conditions": 0.8851569890975952, "join() timeout logic breaks early, leaving processes running after timeout - when timeout occurs on any process, the code executes break which exits the entire for-loop instead of moving to the next process, leaving remaining processes running": 0.9429055452346802, "Flusher per-shard buffers never written to; shared buffer never flushed - each flusher process is given a separate, empty per-shard SpansBuffer that is never written to while all actual data sits in the shared buffer that no process ever flushes": 0.9218020439147949, "process_restarts dict never reset after crash recovery, causing false repeated crash detection - the counter is incremented on crash but never reset after recovery, leading to cumulative counting that can trigger MAX_PROCESS_RESTARTS limit even when process is healthy": 0.49843525886535645, "Per-shard SpansBuffer instances share Redis client with inconsistent assigned_shards - operations like record_stored_segments() assert result lengths against assigned_shards, which can yield assertion errors, wrong metrics, or silent data loss when the shard subset mismatches what Redis returns": 0.7214075922966003, "Backpressure logic now applies across all processes with OR semantics instead of per-process AND semantics - the refactored code raises MessageRejected if ANY process is in backpressure, meaning a single slow shard will pause all incoming spans": 0.8700586557388306, "Original buffer parameter to __init__ is not stored and becomes unused - the buffer parameter is used only once to extract shard count, then discarded while new buffers are created for each process, creating architectural confusion": 0.8431617617607117}